4 Cloud-Native Database Engine Comparative Analysis
Code
+-----------------------------+-------------------------------+-------------------------------+
| Architectural Metric        | Amazon Aurora Global Database | Google Cloud Spanner          |
+-----------------------------+-------------------------------+-------------------------------+
| Core Underlying Model       | Shared-Storage RDBMS (MySQL/PG)| Distributed Shared-Nothing    |
| Replication Mechanism       | Low-latency log-buffer storage| TrueTime API + Paxos Consensus|
| Cross-Region Consistency    | Asynchronous (< 1 second)     | Externally Consistent (Strong)|
| Horizontal Write Scale      | Single-writer node per cluster| Multi-region, multi-master    |
| Recovery Time Objective(RTO)| < 1 minute (Cluster failover) | 0 seconds (Immediate Paxos)   |
| Recovery Point Target (RPO) | < 1 second of data            | Absolute 0 (Zero data loss)   |
| Implementation Fit          | Best for traditional relational| Best for hyper-scale, global  |
|                             | workloads needing low changes.| multi-region active writes.   |
+-----------------------------+-------------------------------+-------------------------------+
Final Cloud Architecture Decision: ApexPay deploys on Google Cloud Spanner for its core global transaction ledger to take advantage of its TrueTime atomic clock synchronization, which guarantees strict external consistency across continents without needing risky manual failover steps.
